From 31a698824474de37d1d2f14dafbfde3cd51ad8a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "keepup[bot]" <keepup[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: move the default OpenAI model off gpt-4.1-nano before it
 shuts down

OpenAI's deprecations page says gpt-4.1-nano shuts down on 23 Oct 2026, in a
notice from 22 Apr 2026, and names gpt-5.6-luna as the substitute. OpenAI
released gpt-5.6-luna on 9 Jul 2026. When nothing is set, the server falls back
to gpt-4.1-nano for settings, chats and agents, so those chats stop working on
that date. Each of those defaults now names the substitute.

OPEN_MODEL_PREF and a workspace's model still win, so nothing a person chose
changes. Commented sample lines and a settings placeholder also name the old
model; they set nothing, so they stay.

Replay date: 1 Sep 2026
Source: https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/deprecations
Source: https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/changelog (9 Jul 2026 entry)
